A||||4||Shaun41178||Underdrive pulley install page complete||||14
Z||000000||Shaun41178||10-15-1999||11:45 AM||||Completed my page on my pulley install.  This pulley is from the Fiero store.  I describe how to install the pulley along with the tools needed and the improvements that it made in the qtr mile.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A> <P>scroll down till you see"underdrive pulley".<P>One thing I forgot to mention on my webpage is that the new pulley does not cause charging problems nor overheating problems.  I noticed a slight improvement in coolant temps on my car perhasp cause the new pulley slowed down the waterpump a little and this helped remove some turbulence.  Maybe but still no overheating problems.  Just thought some people hear would be interested.<P>Let me know what you think.<P>Shaun||||reg||14
Z||000001||GT Bastard||10-15-1999||12:01 PM||||Shaun, you bring new hope to us Automatic guys.  What kindof times can you run without nitrous?  I'd be interested to know.  Next spring I'm planning on taking my 87 Gt to the track.  It's pretty much all stock with a 3.33 gear ratio and an auto.  I'm thinking high 15's. whadya say? later, man..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||10-16-1999||02:36 PM||||Basterd: i run 16.1-16.4 at the track without my nitrous.  I have yet to run in the 15's at a dragstrip without my nitrous but as you can see I have come fairly close.  I am sure a shift kit could get me there.  I have the shift kit but have not installed it yet.  Or perhaps if I just swapped my tranny with the 3.33 I have in my garage i would make it as well.  But that is my winter/spring project.<P>As far as what I think you will run, Most likely low to mid 16's like me.  I would be a little surprised if you did run a high 15 but it is not impossible of course.  A few things to help you get your best time though;<P>1. Thouroughly ice down your intake as I have noticed this is good for about .1-.2 improvement.  <P>2. Disconnect your TCC switch from your bellhousing of your tranny.  Just simply unplug the little blue plug and lay it off to the side making sure it does not come into contact with your exhasut or anything else.  This can be worth about .1-.2 as well.  <P>So best case scenario with these mods is .4 off the qtr.  That is darn good if you ask me.  Or what you could do is run with the TCC plugged in and then run witout it plugged in to see how much of a difference it makes on your car as I am sure that you car might not react as well to this mod as mine has.  <P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-16-1999||07:33 PM||||For those of you making this mod.......<P>SAVE THE BELT LABLES! You'll need them again latter when you have to buy new belts. You won't be able to look it up in a book any more.<P>As for the TCC switch...... make sure you plug it back in latter or you could burn up the tranny. Continuous driving w/o the TC locking will generate significantly more heat in the tranny.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-16-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pretender||10-18-1999||02:01 AM||||slap a bag of ice on your intake! this also gave me a little more in the search for 15's. So far my best is a 16.1.||||reg||6
